# Rust
/target
**/target

# Rust build artifacts
Cargo.lock.*
**/*.rs.bk

# Environment / secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id.json
keypair.json
wallet.json
*.env.local
# ...except the secret-free templates. These are documentation: they carry the
# variable names and the cluster/credential rules, never a value. Without this
# exception `.env.*` swallows them and every operator has to rediscover the
# configuration from the source.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
# Program/deploy keypairs (any naming) — never commit
**/*-keypair.json
*keypair*.json
# Exported/plaintext secret material. `*.key` above does not match a key
# pasted into a .txt, which is exactly how a Phantom import file slipped in.
*secret*
*private-key*
*-key.txt
phantom-import-key.txt

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.next/

# opencode tooling state
.opencode/

# brand-design preview artifacts
.brand-preview/